<title>ITALY: Fantozzi sees Italy in first group of EMU members.</title>
<headline>Fantozzi sees Italy in first group of EMU members.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy will certainly make the first group of nations that will be included in a single European currency from January 1 1999, said Italy's foreign trade minister Augusto Fantozzi.</p>
<p>&quot;I am certain that Italy will be among the first. Others, like the Bundesbank, can advance all the scepticism they like, but the facts speak for themselves,&quot; he said after a conference in Milan.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, Bundesbank council member Hans Juergen Koebnick said that Italy probably will not make the first group of nations joining a European single currency.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
